This is a description of the GOES Satellite Reciever Project.
The document will describe basic operation of device and high-level functional overview.

Basic Idea: use some sort of signal receiver (satellite to LNA etc), passed to
SDR for processing (filtering demodulation), and then use RPI for demodula-
tion/conversion to bitstream. Bitstream is then passed to a FPGA for protocol
decoding, and resulting packets are then passed to another type of microcon-
troller/SBC to convert packets into anything from image data to pure data.
Possibly use 1 RPI for all processing if possible? If too intensive, get another
Microcontroller to split the load for demodulation and data conversion. Inter-
face RPI with laptop for easy display/interaction with data.
